Background: the AttentiveFP abl1/scaffold seed-42 run had stopped at
epoch 15 with train MSE still high (the convergence flag added in N3),
which dragged the cell to RF-significant -0.048.  On 2026-10-12 the run
was redone with the new --min-epochs floor and the cell was
re-bootstrapped, then the campaign summary was updated.

ANNOTATION (2026-10-13, PR #6 finding R1/P1 -- correcting the paragraph
above, which is left as written):
  * "had stopped at epoch 15" conflates two things: the original CUDA
    run EARLY-STOPPED AT EPOCH 35 with best epoch 15 and train MSE 0.57
    (logs/win4070_/win4070_overnight_train_attentivefp_abl1_scaffold_s42.log,
    device=cuda; README.md and docs/methodology.md now say this).
  * "redone with the new --min-epochs floor" misattributes the flip.
    The flip came from the independent rerun ITSELF -- fresh randomness
    on another device (device=mps, printed at line 6 of the stdout log
    cited in Step 1 below); the two runs already diverge at epoch 2.
    The --min-epochs 60 floor never bound: the rerun's longest
    non-improving stretch is 46 -> 62, below patience 20, so it reaches
    100 epochs with or without the floor (README.md, docs/methodology.md).
  * The numbers below (0.6745 / best epoch 82 / +0.020 [-0.018, +0.057])
    are unaffected; only the attribution changes.

